<section class="box-note">
<div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/Organic_Chemistry/Organic_Chemistry_-Part_1_Fundamentals_(Malik)/02:_Representing_organic_structures/2.03:_Organic_nomenclature__-alkanes" class="mt-section"><span id="Skeletal_structure_of_a_straight_chain_may_be_zigzag_or_wiggle-waggle"></span><h5 class="box-legend editable"><span class="lt-icon-default">Skeletal structure of a straight chain may be zigzag or wiggle-waggle</span></h5>

<p>A straight chain alkene is usually drawn as a zigzag line, but rotation is allowed around each single bond, which may change it into a wiggle-waggle line bond structure, as shown in Figure \(\PageIndex{4}\).</p>
